18. What is Code First? Can we create database tables without SQL scripts?

Yes.

In EF Core Code First, we define our database structure using C# classes and DbContext, and EF Core generates the database schema through migrations.

Entity:

public class Product
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; }
    public decimal Price { get; set; }
}

DbContext:

public DbSet<Product> Products { get; set; }

Migration:

dotnet ef migrations add InitialCreate

Apply:

dotnet ef database update

EF Core generates the SQL required to create/update the database.

Flow
C# Entity
   ↓
DbContext
   ↓
Migration
   ↓
SQL generated by EF Core
   ↓
Database
