23. Eager vs Lazy vs Explicit Loading

These concepts are mainly discussed with EF Core navigation properties.

Eager Loading

Load related data immediately.

var orders = context.Orders
    .Include(x => x.Customer)
    .ToList();
Order + Customer
       ↓
loaded together
Lazy Loading

Related data is loaded when the navigation property is accessed.

Conceptually:

order.Customer

causes related data to be loaded when needed, if lazy loading is configured.

Risk

Can cause many unexpected database queries, commonly known as the N+1 query problem.

Explicit Loading

You manually tell EF Core to load related data.

context.Entry(order)
    .Reference(x => x.Customer)
    .Load();
Easy Memory Trick
Eager    → Load now
Lazy     → Load when accessed
Explicit → Developer says when to load
